    "turn_idx": 0,
    "turn_text": "We're here today with Cliff Stern, former Republican Congressman from Florida's Sixth Congressional District, in which he served for 24 years. Cliff is the Executive Director of APCO Worldwide's Washington, D.C. Office, who is the President of the United States Association of Former Members of Congress, which seeks to strengthen Congress, create avenues for bipartisanship, and connect those who have served with those who are currently serving. Cliff is a former chairman of the Transatlantic Dialogue for the European Union, having been the primary liaison between the U.S. House of Representatives and the European Parliament, and he's a former owner of a small chain of motels and restaurants in North Central Florida. He's a former captain in the United States Air Force, a member of the Reformers Caucus at Issues One, and was awarded a meritorious service ribbon in the United States Air Force. Cliff, thank you so much for joining us today. How are you doing?",
