    "turn_idx": 22,
    "turn_text": "the Southern states agreed to that, Northern states agreed, and that allowed them to have population considered for the number of members of Congress from their state. And partly also as a compromise was that the Senate would be elected by the state legislature and not by the people. And that was changed with the 17th constitutional amendment. And the other thing was to have members of the House every two years, and that would force them to go back to the people on a regular basis. So those types of compromise, which were sorted out over a period of time, and at one point Benjamin Franklin thought the whole thing was going to collapse and he asked everybody to pray because they just didn't know where to go and what to do. And so I think if you tell members of Congress that you cannot come to the House or Senate and think it's going to be all your way, And even if you have a small clique of people that all agree with you and maybe just 30 or 40 people, you can persuade, you can change things in the House because if you all vote together, if the majority is very, shall we say, close for the Republicans and Democrats, those 30 or 40 people can change everything. But in the end, they're going to have to realize that even their own party is going to need their votes and they're going to have to compromise. And you don't see that a lot. And without that compromise, nothing gets done. In fact, we can never pass a budget. And it's horrible that today they just voted to pass a continuing resolution only for about three weeks. And back in September, they passed it only for two and a half months. So that means that they can and they even agree to balance the budget in every family in this country balances their budget and most 45 states balance have a constitution amendment to balance the budget. So",
