    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92201.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 26,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. Now, under reapportionment, they took out my hometown. from me so that I didn't have the support. The 24 years of my hometown, I lost by 840 boats. And there were four of us in the primary. And it's interesting, my pole at that point showed me 17-point head. So you can see sometimes you can't count on pole. But the bottom line is the person who won the seat and took my place immediately was against everything and anything and was a contributor that shut down on the government. And it turns out that he campaigned that we should eliminate Obamacare, which I think most Republicans agree with. But there was votes to eliminate portion of it, which he wouldn't vote for because he wanted the complete recension of Obamacare. And so you can't even get some of these tea party people to vote for a compromise where you get, let's say, 30% and it comes back and gets another 30%. They're just too adamant. And of course, In the end, the Obamacare has sort of collapsed because of the tax reform bill that eliminated the demand date for Obamacare.",
