    "turn_idx": 28,
    "turn_text": "for the law is you have to pass budget by october first of that year for the next fiscal year and uh... intel uh... the democrats had when i came in about all seventy percent majority so they could pass anything they want But again, it wasn't until Gingrich took over as Speaker that we actually passed a balanced budget amendment. And frankly, under Clinton, we had surpluses for two or three years and then they all evaporated. But to go to your question is there is so much partisanship today between the Democrats and Republicans and the clique within the Democrats is the Progressive Party and the clique within the Republicans is the Freedom Caucus. Getting all these people together is very difficult. So embarrassingly enough, whether the country is strong or powerful, we can't even balance a budget. And secondly, we can't even pass a budget on time. Not withstanding the fact in the House, all 12 appropriations bill were passed, but they can't get the Senate to pass any of them. So they had to do a continuing resolution. So the Senate has been a little bit more of a problem because there's only 52 senators over there without John McCain voting. There's 51. in the long and short of it. They just can't pass anything there unless they get 51 Republicans of both together.",
