    "turn_text": "You mentioned some of your previous interest in the founding fathers of the United States. In fact, you published books on American political history and everyone and you would well know that prior to the u.s. Constitution we had the articles of the Confederation which had a very weak central government and ultimately led to a failed experiment that needed to be replaced with our current Constitution which had a stronger central government. You see in the European Union right now increasing fragmentation the vote in 2016 for Great Britain to Brexit to leave the European Union? Could you reflect on any possible analyses that might be made between the United States failed attempt of creating a republic under the Articles of Confederation in the late 18th century and the current state of the European Union?",
