  {
    "episode_id": 92201,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92201.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 43,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, Jordan, we had anywhere from 1,000 to 1,200 votes a year. And I feel very proud that I had a consistent voting record. I talked about being a conservative when I ran for Congress in 1988. And I now have a lifetime record with the American conservative union of 95%. And to put it into perspective to have that kind of voting credibility and consistency with so many votes every year is difficult. And so I'm proud of that. And the second thing is that when I came to Congress, I was able to pass 86,000, 86,000 acres that the government owned to return to Florida with Charlie Bennett. He was the Democrat that Congress went to time. And that was part of the Cross Florida Barch Canal, which it was the Nixon administration a project to eventually bring a large canal across from Jacksonville down to Cedar Key. And it collapsed because of environmental concern. So it was a big, these 86,000 acres were returned to",
